Reported by the k103 and k114 workers (reproduced). source remove loads and validates the whole config before removing, so an entry config load refuses (an http:// url that add wrote in v0.4.1 before k110, or a hand edit) cannot be removed by the CLI: exit 1 naming the file; only a hand edit fixes it. Expected: when the config error is in the entry being removed (and only there), source remove drops that entry from the target file and syncs; any other config error still stops it. Document in §7.

2026-09-27 23:31 Reproduced through bin/skilletor (temp HOME/project): user config {sources:{web:{url:'http://host/x.tar.gz'}}}, 'source remove web --force' -> exit 1, '<file>: sources.web.url "http://host/x.tar.gz" must be an https:// URL', file unchanged. Cause: cmdSourceRemove calls load(ctx) (full loadConfig) before the in-use check; any ConfigError propagates. Note: k116's own error text already tells the user 'remove it (skilletor source remove <name>)', which is exactly the command that fails here.

